    {
        "user": "UGWUJUZHT",
        "type": "message",
        "ts": "1776176718.841899",
        "client_msg_id": "a38ac3fe-760b-4c52-9bcd-f8ad14ac83f0",
        "text": "Some thoughts about <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_dhsm0PLOk0|The Computing Historian Recovering Ideas We Threw Away>\n\n\u2022 we finally have asynchronous multi-tasking - i.e. the internet - many independent computers, running at their own speed\n\u2022 we have some of the same \u201cconcurrency\u201d issues, with internet, yet simpler, since internet does not allow actual memory sharing (you can share data, but not memory)\n\u2022 modern computing has been overrun by technical/academic complication, not by UX simplicity\n\u2022 the \u201cnew\u201d invention of CompSci is _not_ \u201cprogramming\u201d but \u201cre-programming\u201d\n\u2022 Design Recovery to lift designs out of old software and to re-express them in code for new RMs - what is the meta-language? (factbases of triples?)\n<https://programmingsimplicity.substack.com/p/some-thoughts-about-the-computing?r=1egdky|...>",
        "team": "T5TCAFTA9",
        "thread_ts": "1776099082.547179",
        "parent_user_id": "UJBAJNFLK",
        "attachments": [
            {
                "from_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_dhsm0PLOk0",
